{"title":"Complex Number Multiplication","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"A complex number can be represented as a string on the form \"real+imaginaryi\" where:\n\nreal is the real part and is an integer in the range [-100, 100].\nimaginary is the imaginary part and is an integer in the range [-100, 100].\ni2 == -1.\n\nGiven two complex numbers num1 and num2 as strings, return a string of the complex number that represents their multiplications.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: num1 = \"1+1i\", num2 = \"1+1i\"\nOutput: \"0+2i\"\n```\n\nExplanation: (1 + i) * (1 + i) = 1 + i2 + 2 * i = 2i, and you need convert it to the form of 0+2i.\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: num1 = \"1+-1i\", num2 = \"1+-1i\"\nOutput: \"0+-2i\"\n```\n\nExplanation: (1 - i) * (1 - i) = 1 + i2 - 2 * i = -2i, and you need convert it to the form of 0+-2i.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- num1 and num2 are valid complex numbers.","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def complexNumberMultiply(self, num1: str, num2: str) -> str:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().complexNumberMultiply","parameters":[{"name":"num1","type":"str"},{"name":"num2","type":"str"}],"returnType":"str","tests":[{"input":["-1+-25i","90+74i"],"expected":"1760+-2324i"},{"input":["-1+-54i","-12+49i"],"expected":"2658+599i"},{"input":["-1+-92i","-41+62i"],"expected":"5745+3710i"},{"input":["-1+18i","31+18i"],"expected":"-355+540i"},{"input":["-1+20i","30+-22i"],"expected":"410+622i"},{"input":["-1+91i","6+66i"],"expected":"-6012+480i"},{"input":["-1+9i","25+-1i"],"expected":"-16+226i"},{"input":["-10+-82i","-69+-9i"],"expected":"-48+5748i"},{"input":["-10+18i","61+63i"],"expected":"-1744+468i"},{"input":["-10+20i","0+-98i"],"expected":"1960+980i"},{"input":["-10+45i","15+-15i"],"expected":"525+825i"},{"input":["-10+54i","58+93i"],"expected":"-5602+2202i"},{"input":["-100+-26i","67+-99i"],"expected":"-9274+8158i"},{"input":["-100+-46i","-97+83i"],"expected":"13518+-3838i"},{"input":["-100+-48i","68+72i"],"expecte